  "description": "Train decision stump base models on bootstrap resampled training sets and aggregate predictions via majority vote.\n\nBagging smooths out high-variance base learners by averaging over empirical bootstrap samples of the training distribution.\n\n### Mathematical Formulation\n$$\n\\hat{y} = \\operatorname{mode}\\left(h_1(x), h_2(x), \\dots, h_B(x)\\right)\n$$\n\n### Step-by-Step Implementation\n1. Generate B bootstrap training samples with replacement\n2. Fit base classifier to each independent bootstrap sample\n3. Combine predictions through majority voting across the ensemble\n\n### Returns\nList of integer class predictions.",
  "theory": "## Understanding the Theory: Bagging Classifier\n\n### Core Intuition: Why Do We Need This?\nIn computational mathematics and machine learning, robust algorithmic routines ensure calculations are both mathematically sound and computationally efficient. **Bagging Classifier** implements a core computational building block.\n\nBagging smooths out high-variance base learners by averaging over empirical bootstrap samples of the training distribution. In this problem, the goal is to: train decision stump base models on bootstrap resampled training sets and aggregate predictions via majority vote.\n\n### Mathematical Principles & Formulation\nThe core governing equation for this operation is:\n\n$$\n\\hat{y} = \\operatorname{mode}\\left(h_1(x), h_2(x), \\dots, h_B(x)\\right)\n$$\n\nEvery term in this formulation plays a precise mathematical role in ensuring dimensional consistency, numerical stability, and correct algorithmic behavior.\n\n### Step-by-Step Computational Workflow\n1. **Phase 1**: Generate B bootstrap training samples with replacement\n2. **Phase 2**: Fit base classifier to each independent bootstrap sample\n3. **Phase 3**: Combine predictions through majority voting across the ensemble\n\n### Practical Machine Learning Applications & Nuances\n* **Algorithmic Complexity**: Designing routines with optimal time and space complexity ensures they scale gracefully to large datasets.\n* **Numerical Accuracy**: Safeguarding calculations against floating-point underflow or division by zero ensures consistent results.\n* **Vectorization**: Implementing operations with contiguous array buffers avoids interpreter overhead.",
