  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef ml_bagging_classifier(X_train: list, y_train: list, X_test: list, n_estimators: int = 5) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Bagging Classifier** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef ml_bagging_classifier(X_train: list, y_train: list, X_test: list, n_estimators: int = 5) -> list:\n    X, y, Xt = np.array(X_train, dtype=np.float64), np.array(y_train, dtype=np.int64), np.array(X_test, dtype=np.float64)\n    N, preds = len(X), []\n    for b in range(int(n_estimators)):\n        idx = np.random.RandomState(b).choice(N, size=N, replace=True)\n        Xb, yb = X[idx], y[idx]\n        th = np.median(Xb[:, 0])\n        lp = int(np.bincount(yb[Xb[:, 0] <= th]).argmax()) if np.any(Xb[:, 0] <= th) else 0\n        rp = int(np.bincount(yb[Xb[:, 0] > th]).argmax()) if np.any(Xb[:, 0] > th) else 0\n        preds.append(np.where(Xt[:, 0] <= th, lp, rp))\n    p_arr = np.array(preds)\n    return [int(np.bincount(p_arr[:, j]).argmax()) for j in range(len(Xt))]\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
